  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array AAA consisting of NNN **distinct** integers (1≤Ai≤2⋅N)(1 \\le A_i \\le 2 \\cdot N)(1≤Ai​≤2⋅N), we have to perform KKK moves.\nWe perform the following steps in one move:\n\n\nSelect an integer XXX such that 1≤X≤2⋅N1 \\le X \\le 2 \\cdot N1≤X≤2⋅N and X≠AiX \\ne A_iX=Ai​ for all iii (X(X(X is not equal to any element of the current array))).\nAppend XXX to AAA.\nThe score of this move =(max⁡1≤i≤∣A∣Ai)−X= (\\max_{1 \\le i \\le |A|} A_i) - X=(max1≤i≤∣A∣​Ai​)−X.\n\nNote that the score is calculated after appending XXX. Thus, XXX can be the maximum element of the array as well.\nFor e.g. if A=[3,1,5]A = [3, 1, 5]A=[3,1,5] and we append X=2X = 2X=2 to AAA, then, AAA becomes [3,1,5,2][3, 1, 5, 2][3,1,5,2] and the score of this move is max⁡([3,1,5,2])−2=5−2=3\\max([3, 1, 5, 2]) - 2 = 5 - 2 = 3max([3,1,5,2])−2=5−2=3.\n\nFind the **maximum sum** of scores we can achieve after performing **exactly** KKK moves.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains three space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the size of the array AAA and the number of moves respectively.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\dots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ denoting the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the **maximum sum** of scores we can achieve after performing **exactly** KKK moves.\n\nIt is guaranteed that it is always possible to perform KKK moves under the given constraints.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤K≤N1 \\le K \\le N1≤K≤N",
      "1≤Ai≤2⋅N1 \\leq A_i \\leq 2 \\cdot N1≤Ai​≤2⋅N",
      "All AiA_iAi​ are distinct.",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
