    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3 1\n1 3 6\n2 2\n1 2\n3 2\n1 2 5",
        "output": "4\n1\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1: We can perform the following move:\n\nAppend X=2X = 2X=2. Score of this move =max⁡([1,3,6,2])−2=6−2=4= \\max([1, 3, 6, 2]) - 2 = 6 - 2 = 4=max([1,3,6,2])−2=6−2=4\n\nHence, the maximum total score is 444.\nTest Case 2: We can perform the following moves:\n\nAppend X=4X = 4X=4. Score of this move =max⁡([1,2,4])−4=4−4=0= \\max([1, 2, 4]) - 4 = 4 - 4 = 0=max([1,2,4])−4=4−4=0\nAppend X=3X = 3X=3. Score of this move =max⁡([1,2,4,3])−3=4−3=1= \\max([1, 2, 4, 3]) - 3 = 4 - 3 = 1=max([1,2,4,3])−3=4−3=1\n\nHence, the maximum total score is 0+1=10+1=10+1=1.\nTest Case 3: We can perform the following moves:\n\nAppend X=4X = 4X=4. Score of this move =max⁡([1,2,5,4])−4=5−4=1= \\max([1, 2, 5, 4]) - 4 = 5 - 4 = 1=max([1,2,5,4])−4=5−4=1\nAppend X=3X = 3X=3. Score of this move =max⁡([1,2,5,4,3])−3=5−3=2= \\max([1, 2, 5, 4, 3]) - 3 = 5 - 3 = 2=max([1,2,5,4,3])−3=5−3=2\n\nHence the maximum total score is 1+2=31+2=31+2=3."
      }
    ]
